# HARNESS ARCHITECTURE RULES

## Scope isolation
- Admin tools MUST be rejected at the registry level if called from client scope.
- Client harness is READ-ONLY + support-ticket creation only.
- Never send API keys, service account JSON, or `.env` values to either harness.

## Audit logging
- Every admin tool call must write a `pending` record to `harness_audit_log` BEFORE execution.
- Update that record to `success` or `error` AFTER execution.

## Auth
- Admin harness requires `X-Admin-Password` header. Return 403 if missing/wrong.
- Client harness has no admin auth but is rate-limited (20 msgs/hour/session).
